    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Artefact reachability — load is not evaluability, and a test is not a caller",
      "prov:value": "`audit:reachability:check` is a step in `code-quality-gates.yml`, so\n`gates.ts` derives it and `bun run cat gates` runs it. `--strict` is not wired: the\nself-declared entry points nothing runs are a backlog, and `failOnNew` is what\nmakes a new one fail meanwhile. Bean `dxqm` holds the day it wires.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean dxqm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Artefact reachability — load is not evaluability, and a test is not a caller",
      "prov:value": "**The wiring arrived in a change of its own, and the seam is the lesson.** The\nscript, its tests and this skill landed first with no step at all, because\n`merge-main`'s resolution push carries no `workflows` scope — so any pull\nrequest touching that file needs a human push on every main-merge round, and 9\nof 20 open PRs were in that state. What could NOT be split is the gate's\n**name** from its **wiring**: `gates.ts`'s `unrunScripts` ratchet refuses a\n`check:` script that appears in no workflow, and it is right to. `1xhc` measured\n21 of 33 such scripts, and `t373` was red on `main` while CI reported green\nbecause nothing ran it. So the alias waited for its step rather than arriving\nahead of it — and while it waited, the skill said in this spot that the gate was\nnot wired, because an unwired gate must never read as a passing one."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Artefact reachability — load is not evaluability, and a test is not a caller",
      "prov:value": "## The two failures this exists to prevent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The two failures this exists to prevent",
      "prov:value": "2026-10-04, found by the merge steward. Both artefacts were declared, both were\ndocumented, and both were past all 217 gates CI runs.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "When a grep fails both ways, narrow the SUBJECT — not the signals",
      "prov:value": "This is the part worth carrying away, because it took two wrong turns to reach\nand both of them looked reasonable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A mention is not a caller, and that distinction decides everything",
      "prov:value": "Measured: crediting every textual mention credits `scripts/merge-queue.ts`,\nbecause `merge-train.bpmn` and `merge-priority.dmn` both name it in their\n`<bpmn:documentation>` prose — and the generated glossary JSON carries that\nprose onward into a third file. **A grep over mentions clears the very defect\nthis tool exists to catch.**"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two unrun states, and one number for both would hide the worse one",
      "prov:value": "**A test is not a caller.** A test proves a module works; it does not make it\nreachable. That sentence is finding 1 in full."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`@entrypoint` — say how you ARE reached",
      "prov:value": "```\n * @entrypoint script:merge:steward\n * @entrypoint none — written for the merge-steward tile, not built yet (bean `xxxx`)\n * @entrypoint spawned by scripts/foo.sh\n```",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xxxx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Commit the relation, print the census",
      "prov:value": "The sidecar holds which decisions are evaluable, which diagrams the resolver\nreaches, which entry points are run, and the gateways pointing at each decision.\nIt does **not** hold module totals or the 710 figure: a census moves on any\ncommit that adds a file, and a gate stale by default is one people learn to\nregenerate without reading. `audit-coverage` paid for that twice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Judge against a baseline; never compare a committed copy",
      "prov:value": "The records live on the `qa-reports` branch (arc `3fva`, owner rulings D1/D4),\nso `<instance>/test/results/` is a **working copy** and not a record. A writer\nwrites it, `qa:publish` pushes the tree once per CI run, and a gate reads the\nbaseline through `judgeQaResult` — `--against <ref>` for the branch, and a\nbaseline that cannot be asked is **`unknown`: reported, never a pass, never a\nfailure.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3fva"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Judge against a baseline; never compare a committed copy",
      "prov:value": "Compose the path with `qaResultPath(root, stem)` and nothing else. Bean `id4s`'s\ndone-when is that **no caller spells `QA_RESULTS_DIR` itself**, so the day the\nworking copy moves it is one line and a grep that proves it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean id4s"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Judge against a baseline; never compare a committed copy",
      "prov:value": "**`failOnNew` is how a soft finding bites.** This gate's first version failed on\nits own sidecar being STALE, as a proxy for the thing it actually wanted: a new\norphan showing up in a diff. The proxy stopped meaning anything the moment the\nrecords left `main` — there is nothing committed left to be stale — and\n`failOnNew` asks the question directly. The standing orphans are inherited and\ndo not fail; the next one fails on the commit that introduces it. If you find\nyourself reaching for staleness to make a backlog visible, reach for this\ninstead."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Provenance",
      "prov:value": "Bean `folio-assistant-dxqm`, under `folio-assistant-1xhc`, written 2026-10-04\nfrom the two failures at the top of this file. Sibling of\n[`audit-coverage`](audit-coverage.md) and split from it deliberately rather than\nadded to it: that skill's subject is a **kind of node** and this one's is a\n**kind of artefact**, and it already carries its own warning about growing a\nsecond subject.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-dxqm",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    }
  ]
